{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_react_pages_phase_4_effects_03_the_dependency_array_the_dependency_array", "label": "The dependency array is not a preference", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/react/pages/phase-4-effects/03-the-dependency-array.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The array declares what the effect reads. It is true or false. Lying produces an effect that reads one render's values forever."}, {"id": "docs_react_pages_phase_4_effects_03_the_dependency_array_cannot_choose_dependencies", "label": "You cannot choose Effect dependencies", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/react/pages/phase-4-effects/03-the-dependency-array.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every reactive value the setup reads must be declared. To remove a dependency you must prove to the linter it is not read."}, {"id": "docs_react_pages_phase_4_effects_03_the_dependency_array_reactive_values", "label": "Reactive values", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/react/pages/phase-4-effects/03-the-dependency-array.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Props and all variables and functions declared directly inside the component. Module constants, setters, dispatch and ref objects are not."}, {"id": "docs_react_pages_phase_4_effects_03_the_dependency_array_stale_first_render_closure", "label": "Omitted dependency freezes the first render", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/react/pages/phase-4-effects/03-the-dependency-array.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each render creates a new setup closure. An empty array means only the first ever runs. The component re-renders; the connection stays on the old room."}, {"id": "docs_react_pages_phase_4_effects_03_the_dependency_array_exhaustive_deps", "label": "react-hooks/exhaustive-deps", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/react/pages/phase-4-effects/03-the-dependency-array.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Computes the correct array from the code. A disable comment converts a compile-time complaint into a runtime stale-value bug."}, {"id": "docs_react_pages_phase_4_effects_03_the_dependency_array_object_function_identity", "label": "Object and function identity re-runs the Effect", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/react/pages/phase-4-effects/03-the-dependency-array.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Object.is fails every render for a new object or function. Depend on primitives, move inside, extract an Effect Event, or useMemo/useCallback last."}, {"id": "docs_react_pages_phase_4_effects_03_the_dependency_array_ref_current_untracked", "label": "ref.current is not tracked", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/react/pages/phase-4-effects/03-the-dependency-array.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The ref object is stable; reading ref.current does not make the effect reactive. That is occasionally correct and also how people hide dependencies."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_react_pages_phase_4_effects_03_the_dependency_array_the_dependency_array", "target": "docs_react_pages_phase_4_effects_01_what_an_effect_is_for_react_dev_useeffect", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/react/pages/phase-4-effects/03-the-dependency-array.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_react_pages_phase_4_effects_03_the_dependency_array_cannot_choose_dependencies", "target": "docs_react_pages_phas